# ============================================================================================
# ops/crontab.manifest -- the desk's scheduler, as source (gap #58)
#
# *** RECONSTRUCTED FROM IN-REPO EVIDENCE 2026-07-29 -- NOT yet verified against the live box.
# *** The operator OWES a `crontab -l` paste + `systemctl list-timers` (register row #58,
# *** deadline 2026-08-05). Until that verification lands, this manifest is the DR FLOOR,
# *** not ground truth: restore-from-GitHub + deploy/reconstitute_cron.sh yields a desk that
# *** RUNS AGAIN, not necessarily a byte-identical twin of the VPS.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (docs/GAP_REGISTER.md:272, row 58): 5 systemd timers were committed but
# the recorder, spot recorder, executor respawn, run_alerts, shadows, the */5 divergence
# sampler and the pgrep self-heals all ran from an UNCOMMITTED VPS crontab -- 119/162 scripts
# had no in-repo scheduler reference, so live and dead were indistinguishable from source and
# a GitHub restore ran NOTHING. This file is the missing half of the desk's genome.
#
# FORMAT (parsed by scripts/check_scheduler_manifest.py; installed by
# deploy/reconstitute_cron.sh):
#   - real 5-field crontab lines for cron-owned jobs ($QUANT_ROOT is set by the installer;
#     on the live VPS it is /home/quant/quant-platform);
#   - `SYSTEMD unit="..." on="..." exec="..."` lines for systemd-owned units (the installer
#     enables committed ones when systemctl exists; exec paths are repo-relative);
#   - every entry carries its EVIDENCE (file:line) and a CONFIDENCE tag:
#       committed-unit      the unit file is in this repo -- schedule is exact
#       documented-cadence  cadence read from dated in-repo observation of the live box
#       inferred            cadence or slot chosen here; only existence/frequency is evidenced
#   - where only the CADENCE is documented, the command SHAPE (log path, flock lock name,
#     exact minute) is reconstructed in the house pattern and is honestly `inferred` detail.
#
# KNOWN GAP, stated loudly: the live box shows ~20-22 active cron lines with flock guards
# (docs/research/deep_sweep/20260729_infrastructure.md:44-45, .../20260729_data-intelligence.md:222-223)
# and 21 quant-* systemd units (docs/research/deep_sweep/20260729_infrastructure.md:171); this
# reconstruction names 17 cron lines and 13 units. The remainder is exactly what the operator
# paste closes -- e.g. the unknown 00:02 writer of deribit_surface/crypto_regime
# (docs/research/deep_sweep/20260729_data-intelligence.md:93-97) is NOT reconstructable from
# the repo and is deliberately absent rather than invented.
# ============================================================================================

QUANT_ROOT=/home/quant/quant-platform

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MONEY-PATH SUPERVISION -- cron plane
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# watchdog: 3-min self-heal tick. Each tick also runs run_alerts.py (the pager),
# run_leverage_opt.py, run_live_combined.py and data_health.py, and heartbeat-gates respawn of
# executor / deadman / liquidations / dashboard / tunnel -- deferring to systemd when a unit
# owns the process (scripts/watchdog.py:57-100; the 2026-07-26 dual-supervision orphan is why).
# The executor's 10-min reconciler is INSIDE the executor process (--interval 600,
# scripts/watchdog.py:187-188; docs/institutional_knowledge.md:328), not a separate cron line.
# EVIDENCE: docs/research/deep_sweep/20260729_infrastructure.md:55-56 ("cron (3-min) ->
#   scripts/watchdog.py"); docs/institutional_knowledge.md:490 ("watchdog.py (cron, every 3min)")
# CONFIDENCE: documented-cadence
# LOCK ported 2026-07-31 from the legacy line (deep-sweep DI-1/infra-F1: two watchdogs, split locks):
# /tmp/watchdog.lock is the lock the legacy twin held; sharing it makes the twins mutually exclusive
# during the migration window and prevents self-overlap after.
*/3 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n /tmp/watchdog.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/watchdog.py >> data/watchdog.log 2>&1

# venue-truth divergence sampler: every 5 min, read-only (calibrates the gap-#19 breaker band).
# EVIDENCE: docs/GAP_REGISTER.md:272 ("the */5 divergence sampler");
#   docs/research/deep_sweep/20260729_data-intelligence.md:77 ("venue_divergence every 5m")
# CONFIDENCE: documented-cadence
*/5 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/run_venue_divergence_shadow.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/venue_divergence_cron.log 2>&1

# RATCHET FENCE (constitution L1.0/L2.0): every measurable property of the desk reported as
# value (floor, distance-to-100%), failing on any regression / unmeasured / unfloored metric.
# --ratchet records improvements only; it can never lower a floor. The 55% -> 90% test-strength
# move of 2026-07-29 is the tempo this fence exists to make permanent and self-initiated.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_ratchets.py (built 2026-07-29); docs/CONSTITUTION.md L1.0
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
7 7 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_ratchets.py --ratchet --json >> data/cro_ai_logs/ratchets.log 2>&1

# KIMI HUNTER (Deep Forest Protocol, waves 1->2->3 enforced in code). BUILT and automated on the
# box per commit a9a4dcd ("cron at 06:00 UTC + full-chain mock proves funding is the only
# remaining variable") but ABSENT FROM THIS MANIFEST until 2026-07-30 -- i.e. live-only
# scheduling, invisible from source, the exact class gap #58 exists to catch. Blocked on
# OpenRouter credit (402); the harness no-ops cleanly without it and fires the moment credit lands.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/kimi_hunter.py:3 ("cannot RUN until OpenRouter is funded"); commit a9a4dcd
# CONFIDENCE: documented-cadence (06:00 UTC from the commit message)
# CADENCE RAISED to maximum sustainable 2026-07-30 (principal: "as frequently as possible for
# maximum exhaustive ROI, optimal and deep"). SIX runs/day at 4-hourly spacing + a WEEKLY DEEP
# sweep. Frequency is deliberately bounded by SPEND, not by a hand-picked number: the monthly
# envelope guard in run_external_panel/panel_budget ($100-150/mo HARD, page-and-abort, never a
# silent quality cut) is what caps real usage, so the cron can be aggressive without risking the
# 2026-07-24 incident class ($21.48 in one day from unbounded resend). Each run executes the full
# wave 1->2->3 protocol; duplicate finds are suppressed by the graveyard + novelty gate, so extra
# frequency cannot manufacture duplicate work.
5 */3 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/kimi_hunter.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/kimi_hunter.log 2>&1
# WEEKLY DEEP: longer budget, targets previously unexplored languages/regions/eras per L1.11a.
35 5 * * 0,3 cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/kimi_hunter.py --deep >> data/cro_ai_logs/kimi_hunter_deep.log 2>&1

