# MAX PUSH (L1.0, principal order 2026-07-30: "every aspect should always aim and hunt to maximise
# itself 100% every single day, believing it never is"). The law already said the gap to 100% IS
# the work queue; what did not exist was the queue. Five separate "what is left" artifacts
# (ratchets, utilisation, enforcement matrix, wiring, gap register) were each true and none
# comparable, so the desk worked whichever one it happened to open. This merges them into ONE
# ranked queue by declared leverage, refreshing its producers first so it ranks today's numbers.
# THE ANTI-COMPLACENCY PROPERTY: it never reports "done". All-green escalates to
# MEASUREMENT-SET-TOO-SMALL, because a system that reaches 100% on everything it measures is
# measuring too little -- and UNMEASURED aspects outrank partially-complete ones, since every
# expensive defect this desk has found lived in something that carried no number.
# Runs LAST in the 06:xx-07:xx governance block so it reads that morning's fresh artifacts.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_max_push.py -> data/max_push_queue.json; docs/CONSTITUTION.md L1.0
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
