# MINER SEATS -- CRON FALLBACK, NO ROOT REQUIRED (2026-07-30). The five seats were systemd-only,
# and installing a systemd unit needs root the operator does not have on this box ("I'm sorry
# quant, I'm afraid I can't do that", measured live during launch setup). A capability the desk
# owns but cannot switch on without an account it cannot access is idle by construction (L1.28a),
# so each timer gets a user-crontab twin at the SAME schedule as its OnCalendar line.
# DOUBLE-FIRE GUARD: each entry first asks systemd whether the real timer is enabled (is-enabled
# is a read query -- no root needed) and stands down if so, so enabling the units later cannot
# double-run a seat; flock guards the seat besides. Grouped with { } so a failed cd can never run
# the seat from the wrong directory.
# EVIDENCE: ops/quant-*.timer OnCalendar lines (dataaxis 14:00, frontier 15:00, prospector 18:00,
#           litminer 19:00, blindrediscovery monthly 1st 20:00); runners ops/run_*_dig.sh
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (cadence copied from the committed timer units)
0 14 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && { systemctl is-enabled quant-dataaxis.timer >/dev/null 2>&1 || flock -n /tmp/seat_dataaxis.lock /bin/bash ops/run_dataaxis_dig.sh >> data/cro_ai_logs/seat_dataaxis.log 2>&1; }
0 15 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && { systemctl is-enabled quant-frontier.timer >/dev/null 2>&1 || flock -n /tmp/seat_frontier.lock /bin/bash ops/run_frontier_rotation.sh >> data/cro_ai_logs/seat_frontier.log 2>&1; }
