# CADENCE MAXIMISATION (principal order 2026-07-31: "maximise and exhaust cadence frequencies for
# everything if it benefits and has ROI, ignoring costs"). Raised above: max-push, promotion
# queue, gen-diversity, constitution core, enforcement matrix, utilisation, timidity 6-hourly
# (each costs seconds of local python; their inputs refresh on the 6h brain/intelligence rhythm,
# so 6h is the point past which extra runs re-read unchanged inputs); gate0 readiness HOURLY for
# the launch window; drills DAILY (19 checks in ~3s -- a free daily proof the rails still hold).
# Two quota-bearing additions below: a 4th daily brain slot and a 2nd frontier dig slot. Both
# reuse the live entries' own flocks, so if the box's crontab still carries the original lines
# the flock makes the extra slot a no-op rather than a double-run.
# DELIBERATELY NOT RAISED, each with its reason: deep sweep stays WEEKLY (8 max-effort auditors;
# its inputs are the week's work -- 2x/wk would re-audit unchanged state at enormous quota cost);
# pull_deploy stays */10 (deploy latency is already below any human reaction time); model upgrade
# stays daily (vendors ship monthly); kimi already at its 6x/day + weekly-deep max, gated on
# OpenRouter not cadence; venue divergence stays */5 (the 2026-07-21 IP ban was over-frequency).
# EVIDENCE: this order; GLOBAL BRAIN MUTEX commit fc7302d (two brains, one tree, one quota)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (flock-guarded against the live twins)
# (2026-07-31: the 45 8 cron twin of the 08:45 systemd timer was REMOVED here -- same minute,
# two launchers, split lock paths (/tmp vs data/), the exact R0048 shape. quant-cro-ai.timer
# owns 08:45; the 2,14,20 slots live in the brain-cycles block above under ONE lock path.)
# refresh_panel_roster weekly dry-run (Mon 05:30) -- adopted from a live-only crontab line
# 2026-07-31 so DR reconstitution covers it; bare invocation is report-only (--apply is manual).
