# MECHANISM ATTRIBUTION (R0137): no sleeve may read as SURVIVED on P&L its stated mechanism cannot
# explain. Built after a live near-miss -- the dashboard showed funding carry as a survivor on
# +24.5pct/Sharpe 13.13 while the funding harvest behind it was 113 dollars of 3,670. A
# cash-and-carry is delta-neutral by construction, so its price legs cancel and its P&L should be
# funding plus basis. The desk's own two-sided carry fence already returned BLEED(inverted) on
# those numbers -- and its verdict gated NOTHING, which is the defect this organ exists to end.
# An unattributed WIN is treated as seriously as a loss: the exposure that produced it is still on,
# still unhedged, and will reverse. HOURLY, alongside the other live-state fences.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_mechanism_attribution.py -> data/mechanism_attribution.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle; caught the live case on its first run)
35 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_attribution.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/check_mechanism_attribution.py --report-only >> data/cro_ai_logs/attribution.log 2>&1

# TRADE REVIEW (R0139): the discretionary desk's LEARNING LOOP, on BINANCE perps. Reads each closed
# paper trade against what was claimed at entry -- thesis, named structure, falsifier, chart state
# -- and against what price then did, then classifies the cause into something actionable
# (THESIS-WRONG / LEVEL-WRONG / TIMING-WRONG / NOISE-STOP / RIGHT-AND-PAID / RIGHT-BUT-TRUNCATED /
# UNLUCKY) and extracts ONE falsifiable lesson. Weights are fixed and nothing here fine-tunes:
# what improves is the desk's evidence-weighted knowledge of WHICH SETUPS PAY, the way a journal
# improves a human. The playbook is an EVIDENCE LADDER -- PROVISIONAL on one observation with no
# authority, SUPPORTED only after 3 agreeing trades, RETIRED the moment one contradicts it (and the
# contradiction recorded so it cannot return), STALE if untested for 25 closed trades. ONLY
# SUPPORTED lessons reach the trading brief: one lucky trade must not rewrite the method.
# 3x/day, offset from the resolver so it reads freshly-closed trades.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_trade_review.py -> data/trading_playbook.json + data/trade_review.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
40 2,10,18 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_review.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_trade_review.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/trade_review.log 2>&1

# COPYTRADING SCREEN (R0140): Stage A, ZERO promotion authority. Two hypotheses live under the
# word "copytrading" and they get opposite verdicts. H1 FOLLOW A LEAD TRADER is NOT TESTABLE from
# public data: the naive split-half test on an OKX leaderboard sample returns Spearman +0.33 with
# 5/6 of the top quintile beating the median, and it is an ARTIFACT -- the cohort is drawn by
# sorting on pnl/aum/copiers/winRatio then measured for performance, blown-up traders are absent
# entirely, mean 45d return across the sample is +81pct (a leaderboard, not a population), and
# n=34 puts rho at ~1.9 sigma BEFORE either bias. It is the exact shape of the 420 patterns
# already killed here. H2 TRADE THE COPY FLOW is measurable: copy capital is FORCED flow, so
# aggregate skew and stress are a crowding gauge that needs no winner picked.
# DAILY, and the cadence is the point: it archives a FORWARD PANEL where traders who DISAPPEAR are
# counted as FAILURES, which is the only unbiased design available. Until two snapshots sit 5+
# days apart the verdict is NO-DATA, never "promising".
# EVIDENCE: scripts/screen_copytrading.py -> data/copytrading_screen.json + copytrading_panel.jsonl
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle; OKX endpoints verified live, Binance 451s here)
50 3 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_copytrade.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/screen_copytrading.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/copytrading.log 2>&1

# SLEEVE ALLOCATOR (R0141): risk across DISCRETIONARY sleeves by MARGINAL growth contribution.
# Adding sleeves only multiplies growth if they are INDEPENDENT -- five sleeves all long crypto
# beta are one sleeve wearing five names, so risk scales with N while growth scales with 1 and the
# desk pays N sets of costs for one bet. Measured on real data this book already shows crypto-vs-
# crypto return correlation +0.48 and gold-vs-crypto +0.15, so the difference between a real second
# edge and a duplicate is large and measurable. Correlation scales TOTAL deployed risk, not merely
# how a fixed total is split: two independent sleeves deploy ~41pct nominal against a 30pct
# correlation-adjusted cap, two duplicates deploy ~30pct. UNMEASURED pairs are assumed DUPLICATE --
# the assumption that costs money when wrong is the one that gets made. Every registered sleeve
# keeps a seed share so it can accumulate the record that would earn it more (L1.28a).
# DAILY, after the resolver has marked the day's closes.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_sleeve_allocator.py -> data/sleeve_allocation.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
25 4 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_alloc.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_sleeve_allocator.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/sleeve_alloc.log 2>&1

# CALIBRATION PROBE (R0142): does this model family's stated probability mean ANYTHING? The whole
# discretionary sizer consumes one number -- Kelly is f*=(pb-q)/b, so if p is noise the sizer is
# not aggressive or conservative, it is ARBITRARY. Checked 2026-07-31 the desk had ZERO resolved
# forecasts: the most consequential input to the money path had never been scored on anything, and
# the sleeve was built to consume it regardless. Calibration is a property of the FORECASTER not
# the strategy, so it is measurable TODAY with questions that resolve from public price data in
# hours -- no capital, no venue keys, ~50 forecasts in two days at the cost of quota alone.
# Every 6h poses 6 directional questions on the sleeve's own instruments (the same KIND of
# judgement it makes when trading, so the calibration transfers) and resolves anything due.
# If Brier lands at or above 0.25 -- the score of always answering 50% -- the verdict is to REMOVE
# the Kelly sizer and run flat size, because sizing on a meaningless number is strictly worse than
# not sizing on it. Feeds L1.29, which the conviction sleeve already reads, so a proven-
# uncalibrated forecaster shrinks its own future size with nobody deciding to intervene.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_calibration_probe.py -> data/calibration_probe.json + .jsonl
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
5 */6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_calprobe.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_calibration_probe.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/cal_probe.log 2>&1

# ORGAN LIVENESS (R0144): is every scheduled organ actually PRODUCING? check_scheduler_manifest
# proves the LINE is installed and check_exploration covers six named hunters; nothing covered the
# other hundred lines. Installed, running and producing are THREE DIFFERENT FACTS and only the
# third is worth anything -- an organ can sit in crontab -l and have emitted nothing for a week,
# which is exactly how a miner goes dark while the board stays green. Reads the cadence and the
# EVIDENCE artifact the manifest already declares on 79 entries, and compares against real file
# age. NEVER-PRODUCED (wiring) is kept distinct from STALE (auth/quota/upstream) because they need
# different repairs. Tolerance is 3x cadence: one missed tick is a hiccup, three is a dead organ,
# and a board that is red most mornings is one nobody reads.
# HOURLY, alongside the other live-state fences.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_organ_liveness.py -> data/organ_liveness.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle; two parse bugs caught by its own tests first)
50 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_liveness.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/check_organ_liveness.py --report-only >> data/cro_ai_logs/liveness.log 2>&1

# PROMOTION GATE (R0150): what evidence buys what expansion, fixed BEFORE the evidence exists.
# The kill condition (R0142) gave the sleeve a defined way to DIE; without this it had no defined
# way to GROW, which makes expansion an improvised decision taken in the mood of a good week --
# the exact moment that decision is worst. THE TRAP IT CLOSES: 50 trades in seven days is ONE
# REGIME, and cadence can manufacture sample size but never calendar time, so every rung requires
# BOTH. RUNG 1 (50 closed + 14 days + hit above the 31.1pct cost-adjusted breakeven + attribution
# clean) raises the per-trade cap from the 6pct floor to measured half-Kelly, still PAPER. RUNG 2
# (100 + 30d + beats buy-and-hold + calibration informative) is the first LIVE money at 1pct of
# book -- small because paper-to-live is where unmodelled slippage appears, and that should cost
# tuition not capital. RUNG 3 5pct, RUNG 4 15pct and that is the ceiling for one sleeve. NO
# SKIPPING: meeting a later rung's counts while failing an earlier benchmark grants the EARLIER
# rung. UNMEASURED never passes -- a promotion granted by a broken reader is the worst failure
# this organ could have. HOURLY with the other live-state fences.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_promotion_gate.py -> data/promotion_gate.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
55 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_promotion.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/check_promotion_gate.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/promotion.log 2>&1

# DISCRETIONARY MAX (R0151): the ceiling-pusher for the discretionary desk -- L1.28c and L1.25a
# applied to this section like every other. TARGET: a 38pct hit rate. That number is LEGAL where a
# CAGR target is not, and the distinction is the whole point: a return figure is reachable by SIZE,
# and size past full Kelly makes growth negative, which is why targeting one corrupts the optimizer
# (PROJECT_HANDOFF 2026-07-12, fenced by R0143). A HIT RATE cannot be reached by sizing at all --
# only by selection, information and filtering, which are exactly the levers the desk wants pushed.
# 38pct is ~one binomial standard error above the 31.1pct cost-adjusted breakeven: the first level
# at which "this works" is distinguishable from "this got lucky". NOT a ceiling -- on reaching it
# the organ RE-AIMS one step further and never reports "target met, stand down" (L1.25a).
# Every cycle it names the ONE binding lever rather than listing ten, because a board listing ten
# produces none. Ladder by leverage: INFORMATION (public charts cannot carry an edge; the event
# sleeve is the non-public version) > CROSS-FAMILY (blocked on the OpenRouter seat) and CALIBRATION
# > SELECTION > ENSEMBLE > EXECUTION. It refuses to idle: every state carries its unlock.
# 4x/day.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_discretionary_max.py -> data/discretionary_max.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
15 1,7,13,19 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_discmax.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_discretionary_max.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/disc_max.log 2>&1

# DISCRETIONARY EDGE HUNT (R0152): find the NEXT discretionary edge, not just tune the current one.
# The section had an optimiser (R0151 pushes the existing sleeve's hit rate) and a learner (R0139
# extracts lessons from closed trades) -- both improve ONE edge, and neither ever asks whether
# there is a second. The allocator's own arithmetic says an INDEPENDENT second edge is worth more
# than a large improvement to the first, because growth MULTIPLIES across uncorrelated bets and
# merely ADDS within one; a desk with a single discretionary hypothesis is one regime change away
# from having none.
# THE FILTER IS THE FORCED-PARTICIPANT TEST, inherited from the event sleeve and the strongest one
# here: every candidate must name WHO has to trade against you and WHY they cannot wait. "RSI below
# 30" names nobody. A hypothesis with no compelled counterparty is a PATTERN, and this desk is
# 420-tested / 0-survived on patterns. Generic answers ("traders", "the market") are refused.
# SIX LENSES on a date-ordinal rotation so coverage is provable: forced liquidity, structural
# lateness, wrong-price anchor, session and calendar, failed expectation, cross-asset divergence.
# All about participants and compulsion, never about indicators.
# ANTI-REPETITION: every candidate is permanently registered and shown back as ALREADY HUNTED. A
# repeat rate over 50pct means the lens is EXHAUSTED and the correct response is to re-aim the
# lenses, NOT to raise the cadence -- a higher cadence on an exhausted space regenerates the same
# ideas faster. Survivors earn a forward clock and a place in the sleeve allocator's independence
# test; they earn no capital (L1.6), and the allocator decides whether a survivor is a real second
# edge or the first one wearing a new name. DAILY.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_discretionary_hunt.py -> data/discretionary_hunt.json + discretionary_edges.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
40 23 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_dischunt.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_discretionary_hunt.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/disc_hunt.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COST HUNT (R0198) -- the one growth lever that needs no proven edge.
# Costs are known BEFORE the trade, they are the whole gap between the 25.0% gross breakeven and
# the 31.1% net one, and near breakeven a third of the cost stack is worth more than a point of
# hit rate. Funding is SIGNED and public: at any moment half the instrument-sides are being PAID
# to hold, and the sleeve was blind to which half. This snapshots the live rate for every
# instrument, ranks paid vs paying sides, and flags the extreme-funding regime the trader's cost
# veto refuses. Selection uses the sign; MARKING stays always-adverse -- different jobs.
# CADENCE IS DATA-BOUND, not chosen: Binance settles funding every 8h (00/08/16 UTC), so a
# snapshot older than one stamp is a different regime's rate. Hourly keeps every read inside the
# 8h freshness contract trade_cost_view declares, with margin for a missed run.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_cost_hunt.py -> data/cost_hunt.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
23 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_costhunt.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_cost_hunt.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/cost_hunt.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRATEGY-FAMILY COVERAGE (R0200) -- what KINDS of edge the miners come back with.
# Every existing coverage organ maps WHERE they look (9 source families x 7 regional seats);
# none mapped what kind of edge returns. Coverage is the count of DISTINCT FAMILIES touched,
# never candidates tested: twelve candidates from one family are correlated by construction, so
# they die together and the desk learns one thing while reporting twelve tests. Names the
# NEVER-HUNTED families as the binding gap, and routes discretionary-adjacent findings to the
# conviction sleeve's playbook as PROVISIONAL -- suggest-only, promoted solely by the sleeve's
# own closed trades. DAILY, ahead of the miner slots so their next dig can read it.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_strategy_coverage.py -> data/strategy_coverage.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
50 5 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_stratcov.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_strategy_coverage.py --import-discretionary >> data/cro_ai_logs/strategy_coverage.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRATEGY-BREADTH FENCE (R0202) -- the clock behind "never limit to just one thing".
# Widened prompts are a REQUEST and the coverage map is a REPORT; neither fails when a miner
# drifts back to the family it knows, which is how breadth actually dies -- one comfortable
# session at a time, with volume never dropping so every dashboard stays green. Fails on NARROW
# (families worked below the floor), UNWIDENED (a hunting surface lost the mandate) and BLIND
# (coverage unmeasured, which can never read OK). The PORTABLE half (--surfaces-only) also runs
# in the law gate at every commit and push, because a mandate leaves a prompt by an edit.
# CADENCE: hourly, right after the coverage map's daily rebuild has had time to land, so the
# measurement it reads is never older than the producer's own cycle.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_strategy_breadth.py -> data/strategy_breadth.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
35 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_stratbreadth.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/check_strategy_breadth.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/strategy_breadth.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRINCIPAL BENCHMARK (R0213) -- does the machine beat the human it was built to copy?
# The desk benchmarks every sleeve against unlevered buy-and-hold because a levered sleeve that
# merely tracks the index takes risk for nothing (L1.6). Same logic one level up: a discretionary
# machine that merely matches the human's own method is engineering for nothing. Re-prices the
# desk's OWN closed trades at his demonstrated 10% risk fraction -- same calls, same entries,
# same stops, only the size changes -- so the difference is attributable to sizing policy alone.
# Exact, not simulated: cost in R is size-independent, so the outcome scales linearly with f.
# CADENCE: hourly, alongside the resolver that produces the marks it reads.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_principal_benchmark.py -> data/principal_benchmark.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
47 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_prinbench.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_principal_benchmark.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/principal_benchmark.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORGAN ER (R0215) -- coma gets TREATED the same day, not counted.
# The desk detected darkness well (check_exploration, check_organ_liveness, check_miner_runway)
# and treated none of it: three organs reported dark for days, every report correct, nothing
# attempted. organ_catchup was the closest thing and treats exactly one disease (quota) across
# six seats. This triages every exploration organ into UNSCHEDULED / BLOCKED / MISWIRED /
# STARVED / CRASHED / UNKNOWN -- because the treatment depends entirely on the cause and a wrong
# treatment is worse than none -- then re-fires what it can and ESCALATES what it cannot with the
# exact blocker. DISCHARGED requires the ARTIFACT to refresh: exit status is the organ's opinion
# of itself and would let a silently-broken organ read healthy forever.
# CADENCE: 4x/day with --treat. Same-day is the standard, so a single daily pass would leave an
# organ dark for up to 24h before the first attempt; four gives three retries inside the window.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_organ_er.py -> data/organ_er.json + data/organ_er_log.jsonl
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
15 2,8,14,20 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_organ_er.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_organ_er.py --treat >> data/cro_ai_logs/organ_er.log 2>&1

# CARRY BASIS-PATH ATTRIBUTION (R0206, 2026-07-31). Re-measures the ONLY deployed sleeve's
# basis-leg behaviour: does ranking perps by funding select into a WIDENING premium (which would
# make the funding harvest compensation for a basis loss) or a converging one? Run 1 REFUTED the
# widening hypothesis (top-4 basis leg +0.65 bps/day, t +3.11; basis leg improves monotonically
# with funding decile), which is what EXONERATED the entry rule and redirected the live -51.74 bps
# price_pnl to execution. That exoneration is a REGIME CLAIM and can expire.
# CEILING TYPE: DATA-ARRIVAL bound, and the arrival that matters is REGIME, not rows -- the panel
# grows daily but the sign of the forward basis path moves on month scales, so a daily line would
# re-read a materially unchanged answer (L1.28c: firing faster than the state changes is waste).
# MONTHLY is the decided cadence, not an inherited one.
# RAISE CONDITION (named, so this is a decision with a falsifier): raise to weekly if any run
# flips the top-decile basis leg negative, or if the book re-arms and live price_pnl diverges
# from this measurement again -- at that point the answer IS moving and the cadence should follow.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/screen_carry_basis_path.py -> reports/carry_basis_path.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
