# FORECAST SCORER (L1.29 calibration). The desk had a forecast LOGGER and no SCORER, so
# check_calibration sat OVERDUE with 7 unscored predictions -- the worst asymmetry available,
# since logging a probability feels like rigour while only the scoring turns it into calibration.
# Resolves "SYMBOL trades above X at +Nh" claims against the CLOSE of the 1m candle containing
# resolve_by (one defined instant, so the answer cannot drift with when the scorer runs).
# Claims it cannot parse unambiguously are left OVERDUE by design and named -- a guessed outcome
# corrupts the measurement the fence exists to protect.
# Hourly at :50 -- the quiz/probe organs log on the hour with 4h and 12h deadlines, so an hourly
# pass grades each one within the hour it matures; denser buys nothing, sparser lets them pile up.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/score_forecasts.py -> data/forecast_log.json (outcomes via fc.resolve)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (first run graded 6 of 7, Brier 0.2484, and left the one ambiguous
