# NET-PROFIT OPTIMISER (principal 2026-08-01: "net profits must always be set to maximum possible
# -- carry holding longer or shorter, size, lower fees"). Measures net PnL per hour held from the
# desk's OWN closed fills, bucketed against the 8h funding grid, with the funding/price/fee
# decomposition INSIDE each bucket -- so a bucket that "wins" on directional drift is visible
# rather than mistaken for carry on a book that is supposed to be delta-neutral.
# Buckets under 12 trades report UNDERPOWERED and are never ranked: ranking thin cells is how a
# book talks itself into a worse parameter.
# Daily 05:25 -- after the 8h settlements land, before the cycle reads state.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/optimise_net_profit.py -> data/net_profit_optimum.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script. First run on 254 trades: 24-48h is the ONLY positive net/hour band
# (+0.00346/h, n=68, 52.9% win); funding rises monotonically with hold (0.039 -> 0.487) exactly as
# theory says, while the price column bleeds -0.155 -> -0.650 -> -1.796 -- a delta leak that SCALES
# with holding time on a book whose price legs should cancel. That leak, not the hold period, is
# the dominant lever. Caveat recorded with the number: the 254-trade sample spans the 07-27 churn
# incident, whose rail-forced closes distort the hold distribution, so the verdict must be re-read
# on post-fix fills before any parameter moves.
25 5 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_netopt.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/optimise_net_profit.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/net_profit_optimum.log 2>&1

# POINT-IN-TIME UNIVERSE SNAPSHOT (R0239). list_perp_symbols filters exchangeInfo to
# status == TRADING and discards the rest, so every backfilled panel is conditioned on the symbol
# SURVIVING to the day the backfill ran -- textbook survivorship bias. First capture (2026-08-01)
# found 851 symbols of which 124 were NOT trading (123 SETTLING, 1 PENDING): 14.6% of the universe
# was invisible to every cross-sectional study the desk has ever run.
# WHY DAILY AND WHY IT CANNOT SLIP: a point-in-time snapshot not taken today cannot be taken
# tomorrow. Unlike almost every other job here, a missed run is not stale data -- it is a
# permanent hole. The value is continuity, so the series only becomes worth something by being
# unbroken. The exchangeInfo call already happens on every ingest and was being thrown away.
# SCOPE, honestly: this fixes the panel FORWARD. It does NOT restore LUNA/UST/FTT/SRM to the
# seven-year history -- that reconstruction from binance.vision delisted archives is a separate,
# larger job and should be scoped once rather than implied here.
# 00:20 UTC: early enough that the snapshot describes the day it is named for, clear of midnight.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/snapshot_universe.py -> data/universe_snapshots.jsonl.gz (append-only)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (first run recorded 851 symbols across 3 statuses)
20 0 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_universe.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/snapshot_universe.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/universe_snapshot.log 2>&1

